# G13 — the twisted prime moments, computed

**The Riemann Hypothesis is not proved.**  Nothing was weakened or assumed:
`RiemannHypothesisFor` and every earlier statement are untouched; there is no
`sorry`/`admit`, no `axiom`, no postulate, no Boolean receipt, no numerical
evidence and no `@[implemented_by]` in any Lean source of this cycle.
`lake build RiemannAnalytic` succeeds (8096 jobs) and `#print axioms` on every
new theorem returns only `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.

The instruction for this cycle was: *stop inventing observers; compute the
actual twisted prime distribution they induce.*  That is what was done.  The
first three moments `S₀, S₁, S₀S₂ − S₁²` of the literal cosh-twisted von
Mangoldt measure are now **proved theorems**, uniformly for every off-line
displacement `0 < |α| < 1/2`, together with matching lower bounds that settle
what those moments can and cannot deliver.

