## 0. Chebyshev lower bounds (new, needed and absent from Mathlib)

* `log_centralBinom_le_psi` : `log (2n choose n) ≤ ψ (2n)`.
* `psi_lower` : `x log 2 − log x − 2 log 2 ≤ ψ x` for `x ≥ 2`.
* `psi_block_lower` : `x/4 ≤ ψ x − ψ (x/4)` for `x ≥ 10⁸`.

The last one is the arithmetic input for everything below: a positive
proportion of the prime mass up to `N` sits in the top log-window `(N/4, N]`.

## 1. `S₀` — the twisted prime mass (milestone 3a)

`vonMangoldt_uniformExponentialTilt` (the master partial-summation estimate the
prompt asked for, in two-sided comparable form):

```
N^{1+v}/16  ≤  ∑_{n ≤ N} Λ(n) n^v  ≤  5.4 · N^{1+v}      (0 ≤ v ≤ 1, N ≥ 10⁸)
```

with absolute constants **uniform in the tilt `v`**.  Specialised to the
functional-equation pair, `twistedPrimeMass`:

```
N^{1+2|α|}/32  ≤  S₀(α)  ≤  5.4 · N^{1+2|α|}             (|α| < 1/2, N ≥ 10⁸)
```

uniformly all the way down to `α → 0` and all the way up to `|α| → 1/2`, as
required.

## 2. `S₁` — the mean log-frequency (milestone 3b)

`twistedPrimeMeanLog`:

```
| S₁(α) − (log N)·S₀(α) |  ≤  123 · S₀(α)                 (|α| < 1/2, N ≥ 10⁸)
```

i.e. `μ_{α} = log N + O(1)`, uniformly in the twist.  Proof: the centered
second-moment bound of §3 plus a pointwise AM–GM at the optimal scale.

## 3. `S₀S₂ − S₁²` — the centered second moment (milestone 3c, the central target)

The master estimate is `tiltedCentered_le`:

```
∑_{n ≤ N} Λ(n) n^v (log N − log n)²  ≤  800 · N^{1+v}     (v ≥ −1/2)
```

proved by a dyadic block decomposition: the mass of the block at log-distance
`≈ 2k` from the top is `≲ N^{1+v} e^{-k}`, and `∑ (k+1)² 2^{-k} ≤ 12`.
Combining with the mass lower bound gives the twisted concentration theorem
`vonMangoldt_twistedCentered_le_mass`:

```
∑_{n ≤ N} w_α(n) (log n − log N)²  ≤  15000 · ∑_{n ≤ N} w_α(n)
```

and hence the theorem the prompt named `zetaTwistedPrimeCenteredVariance`:

```
S₀S₂ − S₁²  ≤  15000 · S₀²                                (|α| < 1/2, N ≥ 10⁸)
```

with the `α²`-carrying corollary `alphaSq_twistedPrimeVariance_le`
(`α²(S₀S₂−S₁²) ≤ 3750·S₀²`) and the relative `o(L⁶)` form
`twistedPrimeVariance_isLittleO_L6`.

**The predicted mechanism is real, and it is proved.**  The cosh tilt does
concentrate the literal von Mangoldt measure in a log-window of *bounded* width
about `log N`, uniformly in `α`, exactly as conjectured; the arbitrary-weight
counterexample of `TiltedLogVariance` does not apply to the zeta weights.

