## 4. What the twisted moments provably cannot do

This is the decisive new information of this cycle, and it is proved, not
conjectured.

### 4a. The relative variance is `Θ(1)`, not `o(1)`

`zetaTwistedPrimeVariance_lower`:

```
S₀S₂ − S₁²  ≥  10⁻⁷ · S₀²                                 (|α| < 1/2, N ≥ 10⁹)
```

Proof: the exact second-difference identity `varForm_eq_double`
(`S₀S₂ − S₁² = ½ ∑∑ wₙwₘ(λₙ−λₘ)²`), then two blocks `(N/4, N]` and
`(N/32, N/8]` which carry comparable twisted mass and are `log 2` apart in
log-frequency.

Together with §3 the relative twisted variance is pinned between `10⁻⁷` and
`15000`, uniformly in `α` and `N`.  So the tilt concentrates the measure into a
window of width `Θ(1)` — but not into a window of width `o(1)`.  **No vanishing
relative budget can come from the shape of the twisted prime measure alone.**

### 4b. At absolute scale the `o(L⁶)` target is false

`twistedPrimeMass` gives `S₀ ≍ N^{1+2|α|}`, so `alphaSq_twistedPrimeVariance_ge`:

```
α²(S₀S₂ − S₁²)  ≥  α² N² / (10⁷·1024)                     (|α| < 1/2, N ≥ 10⁹)
```

and therefore `alphaSq_twistedPrimeVariance_not_littleO`: for any fixed `α ≠ 0`
and any constant `C`, eventually in `N`

```
C (log N)⁶  ≤  α²(S₀S₂ − S₁²).
```

So the literal, un-normalized moments satisfy `α²V ≍ α² N^{2+4|α|}`, which is
polynomially large in `N`.  The target `α² V_prime ≤ δ(T,H)² L⁶` is **only**
available in the normalized form, i.e. after the source divides the prime term
by a factor of size `S₀²`.

### 4c. Consequence for the route

The quantitative answer to the question asked is therefore:

> The twisted prime measure does concentrate (§3), with the predicted
> uniformity in `α`; but its relative log-variance does not tend to zero (§4a),
> and its absolute log-variance is polynomially large (§4b).  Hence the factor
> `δ(T,H) → 0` demanded by `zeta_twistedAnchoredPrime_relative` cannot be
> produced by the twisted prime moments.  It must come from the source
> normalization that relates `S₀` to `L³` in the definition of `D_{ρ,H}` — that
> is, from the still-unproved identification of the literal anchored defect with
> the compensated observable.

This does not close the branch, but it relocates the remaining unknown content
precisely: it is no longer an unproved analytic-number-theory estimate; it is
the source normalization constant.

