## The first unproved theorem, stated exactly

Unchanged from G12, and now the only remaining place where the missing factor
can live:

> **`literalCompensatedAnchorIdentity`.**  For an actual zero
> `ρ = 1/2 + α + iγ` of `completedRiemannZeta` and the actual source local
> matrix at height `T` and window `H`, the literal anchored Gram defect
> `D_{ρ,H}` equals the baseline-subtracted anchored observable
> `𝒜_H(α) − 𝒜_H(0) + R_zero(ρ,T,H)`, with `R_zero = 0` or
> `|R_zero| ≤ η_zero D_{ρ,H}`, `η_zero → 0`, every object being the literal
> source object `γ_ρ, τ_k, φ̂, m_ρ, A_H`.

Everything downstream of it — `literalTwistedPrimeRepresentation`, the relative
remainders, and the high-zero contraction — remains open, and no claim about the
Riemann Hypothesis is made.
